{"kind":"assert","text":"Worktree-discipline audit results and actions taken, completing the board-trust audit (assert 1216de75). 73 worktrees existed against ~25 live commitments; 60 served no live lane. Root cause is structural: AGENTS.md step 6 triggers cleanup only on merge, but 31 of 72 lane worktrees ended without one (cancelled, withdrawn, or superseded by a recut), so nothing ever prompted removal; recut chains left up to six checkouts per lane family.\n\nACTIONS TAKEN by planner today, under hugh's session directive: removed 19 worktrees independently re-verified clean with heads contained in main (including six under /private/tmp and one under /private/var/folders); pushed 8 local-only branches to origin so their heads survive ref loss (ui-notification-dropdown, github-proposal-commitment-chain, mcp-late-actor-recut, mcp-review-guard-recut, merge-all-live-succession, review-guard-authority-current, sealed-receipt-directional-resume, ui-event-addresses — the last two are recovery-lane deliverables under requests a3f62a52 and a246974b). Nothing dirty, active, or unmerged was touched.\n\nDATA AT RISK — needs an ownership ruling, not deletion. Three worktrees hold work that exists on no ref anywhere: (1) gitseq-worktrees/canonical-authority-eventids — 242 uncommitted insertions across 16 files implementing ValidateAuthorityEventID plus SKILL.md and seven reference pages; zero board trace, zero commits on any ref; the branch head equals main so the ref preserves nothing. (2) gitseq-worktrees/security-gates — 212 uncommitted test lines, three named ciguard test functions on no commit anywhere. (3) gitseq-worktrees/custody-reconcile — mid-cherry-pick with two UU conflicts; only the partial resolution is unique. Per the one-writer rule these need their author identified and a decision to commit or discard; planner will not remove them.\n\nREMAINING CLASSES: 31 clean worktrees on settled lanes are removable at any time with refs kept (list reproducible: any worktree whose branch has no non-settled commitment). 12 are active — note the duplicate-checkout hazard: three checkouts at b1daa567, two at 86af0f87 (one dirty with a test mutation), triplicate review-stale checkouts at c9280b32 already declared history by request #12614. Four worktrees exist solely to hold one-line test mutations and should be created and destroyed inside test runs. One refless commit edde4a62 sits under /private/tmp and will not survive a reboot; it is a near-duplicate mutation scratch of live head 86af0f87.\n\nPOLICY input for proposal c781f3f5 item 6: record body.worktree beside body.branch in promises; gs merge receipts name the lane worktree as removable; request retirement surfaces any worktree on the retired lane as unowned; refuse a second worktree at a live lane's head; a periodic gate flags worktrees whose branch has no non-settled commitment and heads reachable from no ref."}